            run_end = matches[j].1;
            j += 1;
        }
        grouped_runs.push((run_start, run_end));
        i = j;
    }

    // Now need to decide if we are in greedy/compress mode or normal. For JSON tests, -g gave collapsed empty fields even for regex.
    // So for normal regex split, we should NOT group, but keep each individual match.
    // For greedy/compress, group.

    // However our function currently doesn't know flags; caller will decide. For simplicity, we will have a parameter later.

